# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Grand Mahjong Master-Key — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values for your own host.
# NEVER commit the real `.env`. This file contains NAMES ONLY — no secrets.
#
# Important: the site runs with NONE of these set. Every variable below has a
# safe default or an unused code path. See MIGRATION.md section 4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Runtime -------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the Express server binds to. Defaults to 5173 if unset.
# Most hosts (Cloud Run, Render, Railway, Heroku, Fly) inject this for you —
# do not hardcode it in your own host config unless you run on a bare VPS.
PORT=5173

# Must be exactly `production` for the built server to serve dist/public
# instead of booting the Vite dev middleware. The `npm start` script already
# sets this, so you only need it here if you launch `node dist/index.js`
# directly (e.g. in a Dockerfile CMD or a systemd unit).
NODE_ENV=production


# --- Postgres (OPTIONAL — not required to run the site) -------------------
# Only read by server/db.ts, which is only reached by POST /api/orders.
# No page in the frontend calls that endpoint today: all payments happen on
# Shopify, so the funnel works with no database at all. Leave this unset
# unless you intend to start recording orders yourself.
# Format: postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE
# DATABASE_URL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT environment variables — documented here so nobody goes looking for them
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# META PIXEL ID (1666692734460053) is intentionally hardcoded, in two places
#   that must always match:
#     - client/index.html   (base snippet, `fbq('init', ...)`)
#     - client/src/lib/pixel.ts  (the PIXEL_ID constant)
#   A pixel ID is public by design — it ships in the HTML of every page — so
#   there is no security reason to move it into an env var, and doing so would
#   split one value across two build systems.
#
# SHOPIFY CART PERMALINKS are hardcoded in the checkout pages. They are public
#   URLs, not credentials. Do not move them to env vars: each one encodes a
#   specific variant ID and quantity, and a typo silently sells the wrong
#   product. Full catalog in HANDOFF.md section 2.
#
# There are NO API keys, tokens, webhook secrets, or private credentials in
# this project. Nothing in the code authenticates against Shopify or Meta.
